Keywords: benefits of test automation, maintenance overhead, risks of test automation, test automation, vendor lock-in.

1. **Benefits of Test Automation** (ISTQB CTFL v4.0.1):
- **Time savings on repetitive tasks**: speeds up execution of repetitive checks (especially regression and smoke suites) and frees human testers for deeper test design, risk analysis, and exploratory testing;
- **Consistency and repeatability**: executes the exact same steps/inputs reliably, reducing simple human execution errors;
- **Objective metrics and faster feedback**: makes coverage, test results, and build/pipeline feedback available quickly (especially in CI/CD).

2. **Risks of Test Automation and Exam Traps**:
- **Unrealistic expectations and inaccurate effort/cost estimates**: underestimating initial scripting, test data setup, environment stability, and ongoing script maintenance when UI or APIs change;
- **Automating the wrong things**: trying to automate unstable features, one-off checks, or areas where human judgment/exploration is far more effective;
- **Over-reliance on tools**: assuming automated pass rates mean the product is bug-free or that automation replaces human critical thinking, domain insight, and exploratory testing;
- **Technical and vendor risks**: **vendor lock-in** or vendor abandonment, **open-source** library/tool maintenance or compatibility issues, platform/environment incompatibility, and **non-compliance** with regulations or safety standards.
